# Database Design (hard rules)

Hard constraints for schema / migrations / TypeORM entities. Prefer this file for **new** database mandates.

Related: `date-time-format-standard.mdc` (API wire format after column type is chosen); `migrations-stable-manual-only.mdc` (where to put SQL).

## Date / time columns (mandatory)

**Default: always use `timestamp with time zone` (`timestamptz`).**

Applies to any calendar time, deadline, expiry, start/end, created/updated business timestamps, and similar.

| Do | Do not (unless developer explicitly opts out) |
|----|-----------------------------------------------|
| `timestamp with time zone` / TypeORM `type: 'timestamp with time zone'` | `date`, `timestamp` without time zone, `timestamp without time zone` |
| Store UTC; convert at edges via merchant timezone utils | Rely on DB/session local time or implicit offsets |

**Exception:** use PostgreSQL `date` (date-only) **only** when the developer **explicitly** says so (e.g. “只要日期不要时区”, `revenueDate`-style day ledger). Never choose `date` by default.

Wire format after type is chosen:

- `timestamptz` → Type 2 in `date-time-format-standard.mdc` (`timeZoneToUtc` / `utcToTimeZone`, ISO)
- explicit `date` → Type 1 (`YYYY-MM-DD`, no TZ shift)

```sql
-- BAD (default path)
expire_date date NULL;

-- GOOD
expire_date timestamp with time zone NULL;
```

```typescript
// BAD
@Column({ type: 'date', name: 'expire_date', nullable: true })

// GOOD
@Column({ type: 'timestamp with time zone', name: 'expire_date', nullable: true })
```

## Migrations placement

- New SQL only under `xituan_backend/migrations/` with the **next** numeric index.
- Do **not** edit `migrations_stable/` as part of AI implementation.

